chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Controlling the keyboard and mouse for an advanced course: chapter 23 and today's PyAutoGUI, PyScreeze, PyMsgBox, MouseInfo and the input paths of X11, Windows and macOS"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-13T20:00:00; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.6." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45, chx:P46, chx:P47, chx:P48, chx:P49, chx:P50, chx:P51, chx:P52, chx:P53, chx:P54, chx:P55, chx:P56 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does chapter 23 of the 3rd edition teach about controlling the mouse and keyboard with PyAutoGUI (the pauses and fail-safes, the coordinates, moving, clicking, dragging and scrolling, MouseInfo, screenshots, pixel colors and image recognition, window objects, typing, key names and hotkeys, tips for GUI scripts, message boxes and the practice programs), which of its 25 listings, printed outputs and statements still hold under Python 3.14.6 with PyAutoGUI 0.9.54 and its newest companion packages, how do other Python, Tk, PyScreeze, Pillow and PyMsgBox releases change them, how do the three operating systems and the X11 and Wayland sessions let a program send input, and what must an advanced course correct or add so that it matches the packages, the platforms and the files the book ships?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-13." .
