chx:F1 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Background"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Chapter 23 of the 3rd edition, Controlling the Keyboard and Mouse, teaches PyAutoGUI (the fail-safes, moving, clicking, dragging and scrolling the mouse, the MouseInfo application, screenshots, pixel colors, image recognition, window objects, typing and key names, hotkeys, tips for GUI scripts and message boxes) and ends with 13 practice questions and 3 practice programs [P01]. The page was fetched on 2026-10-13 and returned 200 with 103,072 bytes, holds 25 listings, 6 figures and 1 table, and its sha256 equals the chapterDigest the book's own chapter ontology records [P01] [P03] [P04]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P03, chx:P04 .
chx:F2 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The online materials"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The online materials of the 3rd edition (7,759,877 bytes, 91 files, 72 of them Python) hold spiralDraw.py (580 bytes, 15 lines) as the only file that imports pyautogui and five files that import pyperclip (alternatingText.py, ccwd.py, cliprec.py, phoneAndEmail.py and showmap.py), and none of pyautogui.py, submit.png, screenshot.png or mouseInfoLog.txt, which the chapter names; the publisher's book page has 1 occurrence of Controlling the Keyboard and Mouse and 0 of PyAutoGUI [P01] [P02] [P04]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P04 .
chx:F3 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "No release 1.0.0"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter attaches behaviour to PyAutoGUI 1.0.0 in 3 passages (locateOnScreen returning None before it, window features working only on Windows as of it, and the same note in the practice program), but PyPI lists 50 releases of PyAutoGUI with 0.9.54 (2023-05-24) as the newest and no 1.0.0, while PyScreeze, which does the locating, has 1.0.0 and 1.0.1 (both 2024-08-20) among its 29 releases; the installed set was PyAutoGUI 0.9.54, PyScreeze 1.0.1, PyMsgBox 2.0.1, PyTweening 1.2.0, PyGetWindow 0.0.9, MouseInfo 0.1.3 and python3-xlib 0.15 [P01] [P16] [P17]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P16, chx:P17 .
chx:F4 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The chapter replayed"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The 25 listings of the chapter hold 80 statements; replayed as printed, 40 of the 80 matched the book's output with Python 3.14.6 and the newest packages (52 ran without an exception and 28 raised), 40 without OpenCV, 41 with PyScreeze 0.1.28, 40 under Python 3.12.3 with Tk 8.6.14 (53 ran and 27 raised) and 1 in an empty environment; the statements that differ are the pointer positions, the pixel((50, 200)) call, the Box values, the window objects, mouseInfo() and the spiralDraw.py listing, which raises IndentationError as printed [P01] [P05]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P05 .
chx:F5 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Pauses and fail-safes"@en ; sen0414:findingText "PAUSE is 0.1 and 15 action functions pause after the call, 14 of them once and rightClick twice, while position, size, screenshot, pixel, onScreen and sleep do not; the corners (0, 0), (1919, 0), (0, 1079) and (1919, 1079) make the next call raise FailSafeException but moveTo(0, 0) itself returns, and afterwards position, size and screenshot still run while click, write and moveTo raise; FAILSAFE_POINTS is computed at import, so after the screen was resized from 1920 by 1080 to 1280 by 720 the running process kept the old corners (MEASURED single runs with PyAutoGUI 0.9.54) [P01] [P07] [P08]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P07, chx:P08 .
chx:F6 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Windows-only window functions"@en ; sen0414:findingText "On Linux none of the 6 window functions (getActiveWindow, getAllWindows, getWindowsAt, getWindowsWithTitle, getAllTitles and getActiveWindowTitle) exists in pyautogui 0.9.54, importing pygetwindow 0.0.9 raises NotImplementedError, PyAutoGUI 0.9.40 does not import at all, and both the PyAutoGUI documentation (Windows-only, currently) and the PyGetWindow README (only the Windows platform is implemented) say so; the chapter's listings 17, 18 and 19 therefore raise at their first getActiveWindow call [P01] [P07] [P23]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P07, chx:P23 .
chx:F7 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Silent key names"@en ; sen0414:findingText "press('nokey'), press('SHIFT'), keyDown('nokey') and hotkey('ctrl', 'nokey') raised nothing and typed nothing, write(['a', 'nokey', 'b']) typed ab, write('café') typed caf, an emoji vanished and write(12) raised TypeError; KEYBOARD_KEYS holds 194 names, every one of the 41 names of Table 23-1 and its text is in it, f13 and f24 exist and the capital A is not in the list, and the roadmap lists a strict mode as a plan (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P10] [P14]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P10, chx:P14 .
chx:F8 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Scroll units"@en ; sen0414:findingText "scroll(-1), scroll(-2), scroll(-3) and scroll(-10) moved a text widget by 1, 3, 5 and 19 lines under Tk 9.0.3 and by 2, 5, 8 and 29 lines under Tk 8.6.14, while scroll(3) sent 3 presses of button 4, scroll(-2) 2 of button 5, hscroll(2) 2 of button 7 and hscroll(-1) 1 of button 6, so the chapter's advice to experiment holds (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P09] [P27]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P09, chx:P27 .
chx:F9 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Exact image matching"@en ; sen0414:findingText "A button cut from the screen was found at (400, 300, 84, 35); the same image with one black pixel raised ImageNotFoundException, as the chapter says, and so did grayscale=True, confidence=0.9 found it only with OpenCV installed and raised NotImplementedError otherwise, the same button at a larger font, 109 by 45 pixels instead of 84 by 35, was not found, and a Box holds np.int64 with OpenCV and int without it (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P11] [P50]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P11, chx:P50 .
chx:F10 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "A missing image"@en ; sen0414:findingText "With PyScreeze 0.1.27, 0.1.28 and 0.1.29 a missing image returns None and click('submit.png') raises TypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable NoneType object, while with 0.1.30, 1.0.0 and 1.0.1 it raises ImageNotFoundException, so the change is at PyScreeze 0.1.30; PyAutoGUI 0.9.41 with PyScreeze 1.0.1 and 0.9.40 do not import, and hold() exists from 0.9.54 and not in 0.9.41 or 0.9.50 (MEASURED single runs) [P11] [P16] [P17]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P11, chx:P16, chx:P17 .
chx:F11 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The pixel call"@en ; sen0414:findingText "pixel(0, 0) returned RGB(red=176, green=176, blue=175) as the chapter prints, but pixel((50, 200)), the second form the chapter prints, raised TypeError: pixel() missing 1 required positional argument: 'y'; pixelMatchesColor was True for (130, 135, 144), False for (131, 135, 144) and True with tolerance=1, and a display of depth 16 returned (172, 174, 172) for a background of (176, 176, 175) and failed the match (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P11] [P18]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P11, chx:P18 .
chx:F12 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "MouseInfo and Tk 9"@en ; sen0414:findingText "pyautogui.mouseInfo() ended with TclError: bad option 'variable' under Tk 9.0.3 (Python 3.13.14 to 3.15.0b4) and ran under Tk 8.6.14, where F6 with the 3 Sec. Button Delay on logged 1600,850 after the pointer had moved from 1500,800, and with the delay off logged 1500,800, 1600,850 and 1700,900; the Tcl 9.0 manual documents trace add variable and not the old trace variable (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P24] [P40]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P24, chx:P40 .
chx:F13 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "XTEST and sent events"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Input from PyAutoGUI reached an X window with send_event False through the XTEST extension, the letter q sent with XSendEvent arrived with send_event True, and xterm discarded the 2 keystrokes ab sent with XSendEvent, received cd from PyAutoGUI and received ab only with allowSendEvents true (MEASURED single runs) [P31] [P32] [P42] [P56]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P42, chx:P56 .
chx:F14 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Backends and permissions"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The 3 backends name SendInput, mouse_event and keybd_event (Windows), CGEventPost and Quartz (macOS) and fake_input of XTEST (Linux); with XDG_SESSION_TYPE set to wayland a screenshot raised PyScreezeException while moveTo(300, 200) still worked through X; Windows documents SendInput as subject to UIPI and macOS asks for the accessibility permission, and none of the 3 input paths other than X11 ran here (NOT EXECUTED) [P33] [P35] [P36] [P38]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P33, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P38 .
chx:F15 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The spiral"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter's spiral loop made 32 drag calls, the first five (300, 0), (0, 280), (-280, 0), (0, -260) and (260, 0), and drew inside the box (180, 129, 481, 411); the shipped spiralDraw.py (580 bytes, 15 lines) drew inside the same box and exited with 0, but it calls dragRel, waits with time.sleep(5), sets LOG_SCREENSHOTS and uses a duration of 0.1 where the chapter prints drag and 0.2 (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P02]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02 .
chx:F16 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Message boxes"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Enter on alert and on confirm returned 'OK', Escape on confirm returned 'Cancel', prompt returned '' for Enter alone and None for Escape, password returned 's3cret', and confirm with timeout=1500 returned 'Timeout' after about 1.5 seconds; the installed PyMsgBox 2.0.1 says __version__ 1.0.9, and its signatures carry type hints that 1.0.9 lacks (MEASURED single runs) [P12] [P19] [P20]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P12, chx:P19, chx:P20 .
chx:F17 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Looking busy and the idle time"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The X idle time was reset by move(1, 0) and press('shift') (under 0.4 seconds) and not by position(), size() or screenshot() (over 1 second); a script that moved the pointer 1 pixel left and right three times made the x positions 799, 800, 799, 800, 799 and 800 and the idle time fell from above 2 seconds to below 1.5 seconds (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P48]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P48 .
chx:F18 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Appendix B"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The answer to question 6 types Hello world! without the comma of the question, the answer to question 13 misspells pyautogui as pyatuogui (NameError) and calls activate on a list, and the answer to question 1 says to move the mouse to any corner, which raises FailSafeException in the next call; the answers to 13 questions were read on the page, 252,727 bytes [P06]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P06 .
chx:F19 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Interpreters and releases"@en ; sen0414:findingText "One program of 27 items ran under 12 interpreter rows: Python 3.12.3, 3.13.14, 3.14.2 to 3.14.6, 3.15.0b4 and 3.14.6 with OpenCV ran every item, 3.14.0 and 3.14.1 raised TclError: Can't find a usable init.tcl, and 3.11.17 had no tkinter; 14 of the 27 items differed between some pair of rows; across 14 PyAutoGUI and PyScreeze combinations 7 items differed, across 7 Pillow releases (9.5.0 to 12.3.0) 3 items differed only by a DeprecationWarning in 12.3.0, and across 3 PyMsgBox releases the signatures differed [P20] [P30] [P54] [P55]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P20, chx:P30, chx:P54, chx:P55 .
chx:F20 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Coordinates, steps and monitors"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Points outside the screen are clamped by the X server, (-50, -50) giving (0, 0) and (5000, 5000) giving (1919, 1079), while (40000, 500) raises struct.error; a move of duration 0.25 made 6 motion events and 1.0 made 21; with 2 virtual monitors added xrandr listed 3 monitors and size() still said (1920, 1080), which fits the documentation that only the primary monitor is handled (MEASURED single runs) [P01] [P07] [P09]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P07, chx:P09 .
chx:F21 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The links of the chapter"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Of the 13 external links of the chapter, 7 answered 200, 3 answered 302 with a Location (the Udemy course, mouseinfo.readthedocs.io and pyautogui.readthedocs.io), youtu.be answered 303 and then 429, the sushigoroundbot repository answered 403 through the proxy of this study, and sumopaint.com was unreachable with an SSLError [P01] [P43]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P43 .
chx:F22 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Not executed"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Nothing ran on Windows or macOS, with the accessibility permission, with a real Wayland compositor, on real or multiple monitors, with HiDPI scaling, on a real screen, in the Sushi Go Round game, against a captcha, or with a real instant messenger; Python 3.15 was only the beta 3.15.0b4; and the photograph was not fetched because the single request to Wikimedia Commons answered 429 [P01] [P36] [P43] [P55]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P36, chx:P43, chx:P55 .
chx:Scorecard a sen0414:QualityScorecard ; rdfs:label "Quality scorecard"@en ; sen0414:topicCoverage "79 primary-source concepts inventoried from the textbook ontology." ; sen0414:citationStrength "56 sources, all opened and verified at 2026-10-13T20:00:00; 36 cited by findings." ; sen0414:methodologyCompliance "RDODI procedure v1.6.0 Stage 1." ; sen0414:reproducibility "Every source is a stable public URL; every claim names its sources." .
